# Independent manual rejection checks, not a Run All script. Use disposable local accounts.
# Sign out first and retain the anonymous cookie/CSRF pair. See auth.http and HTTP-GUIDE.md.
# Each file has its own variables. Real tokens/passwords belong only in private settings.
# 20 account requests/minute/source IP; 429 can supersede expected outcomes below.
@baseUrl = https://localhost:7240
@csrfToken = REPLACE_WITH_CURRENT_ANONYMOUS_CSRF_TOKEN
@email = REPLACE_WITH_CONFIRMED_LOCAL_EMAIL
@unconfirmedEmail = REPLACE_WITH_UNCONFIRMED_LOCAL_EMAIL
@unconfirmedPassword = REPLACE_WITH_UNCONFIRMED_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD
@newPassword = REPLACE_WITH_VALID_NEW_PASSWORD
@resetToken = REPLACE_WITH_VALID_UNUSED_RESET_TOKEN
@userId = REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_USER_GUID

### N1. Prepare anonymous CSRF for checks that require valid headers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/csrf

### N2. Missing CSRF on login: 400, before credential validation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "intentionally-wrong" }

### N3. Invalid CSRF on reset request: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: deliberately-invalid

{ "email": "{{email}}" }

### N4. Unknown reset-request email: 202, no private file should be created
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "does-not-exist@example.invalid" }

### N5. Unconfirmed account reset request: 202, no reset file should be created
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "{{unconfirmedEmail}}" }

### N6. Incorrect password: 401 generic response
# A failure increments Identity's failed-access count. Do not repeat on an account you need.
# Five failed attempts can lock the account for 15 minutes; correct login then also fails.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "intentionally-wrong" }

### N7. Correct password, unconfirmed email: 401 generic response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "{{unconfirmedEmail}}", "password": "{{unconfirmedPassword}}" }

### N8. Invalid reset token: 400; password stays unchanged
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "{{email}}", "token": "intentionally-invalid", "newPassword": "{{newPassword}}" }

### N9. Weak replacement password with a valid unused reset token: 400
# Obtain a valid reset token with identity-recovery.http R2 first; do not log in between.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "{{email}}", "token": "{{resetToken}}", "newPassword": "short" }

### N10. Invalid confirmation token: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/confirm-email
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "userId": "{{userId}}", "token": "intentionally-invalid" }

### N11. Anonymous session read: 401 (no redirect)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/session

### N12. Anonymous logout: 401 (no redirect)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### N13. Invalid email format: 400 validation response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "not-an-email" }

# Additional manual cases:
# - In a second private cookie jar, verify a CSRF header from the first jar fails (400).
# - Request a reset, change password successfully, then replay that reset token (R4: 400).
# - For expiry, retain a token beyond the configured provider lifespan; expect reset 400.
# - To examine rate limiting, repeat N1 until this IP's account budget is exhausted (429).
# - Test Production mail routes separately: register/forgot/resend must return 503 with valid CSRF.
# - Account closure: see identity-closure.http; use a disposable account, not direct SQL deletion.
